e predicates are made satisfiable-by-construction via a byte-level artifact schema (§6.1) plus a conformance table naming each predicate's failure trap (§6.2).\n\n## The four design decisions that carry the most weight\n\n**1. The review doc is an entry point, not the corpus.** A8's claim is about artifacts spread across L06/L08/L11 + the decision and scar graphs (SAEOS-1 §6.1b). Extracting from `*_review.md` alone would score `Constraint`, `Component`, and `TradeOff` as absent for reasons unrelated to prose structure — a **false NO-GO** that kills a viable S1. So the design adds a `LOCATE` component and splits absence into `absent-in-source` (falsifies A8) vs `absent-out-of-corpus` (a corpus-assembly work item), with distinct verdict bases.\n\n**2. `Outcome` is excluded by construction.** §4.3 says it's *\"the only node type that may be created long after its subject\"*; §6.1b routes it to L17/L19 and §8 to slice S3. Scoring it at S1 would manufacture loss that isn't extraction failure.\n\n**3. Anti-rigging is the spine of the design.** Exclusions launder loss, single extractors read structure into prose, and good averages hide dead spines — so: exclusions need a spec citation *and* a default policy and may only shrink; goal 3 is extracted twice blind with an ≥0.80 agreement floor; and Decision-`chosen`/`rationale` (C2) and Scar 6-field round-trip (C3) are hard gates independent of the ratio. Thresholds are pre-registered with a justification derived from what slice S2 needs, and amending them after extraction starts voids the probe (`VOID` state).\n\n**4. The acceptance regex has two traps I specified rather than papered over.** `^loss_ratio: 0\\.[0-9]+$` admits only [0.0, 1.0), so total loss is unrepresentable; and if no node is instantiable at all (`D = 0`) there's no honest value. Emitting `0.00` there would read as *zero loss* — the strongest GO signal — to make a grep pass. The design forbids it and specifies reporting the gate as **unsatisfiable, not unsatisfied**.\n\nTwo things I flagged rather than resolved: `constitution/README.md` describes B0.0 as *\"directory skeleton only\"*, so the three named goals may be too thin to carry real decisions — handled by a pre-registered diversity guard that adds a G4 only on a stated trigger. And the probe tests a threshold (≤0.35) deliberately weaker than §8 S1's ratified `lossless`; if extraction lands between, the output is a **proposal to amend §8 S1**, routed for ratification, not an edit to the spec.","ttft_ms":2210,"ttft_stream_ms":1447,"time_to_request_ms":99,"type":"result","duration_ms":421933,"uuid":"59fd1362-073a-4a8d-8a9a-8133d370669f"}
